  "articleBody": "Tackling garage upgrades can seem straightforward until you run into complex wall assemblies or utility lines. Here is when to call a professional contractor: Signs you need expert support: - Your garage shares walls or a ceiling with occupied bedrooms, requiring specific fire-rated drywall and air sealing. - You notice persistent moisture, damp concrete, or active roof and wall leaks that must be resolved prior to closing cavities. - Your upgrade involves new custom framing, modifying load-bearing elements, or running concealed wiring. - The home was built before 1978, meaning painted surfaces could involve lead-safe work practices and certified handling. - Multiple trades are involved, including framing, drywall, electrical, and finish trim. What Can Change the Right Choice: Climate exposure and how you plan to use the space dictate whether standard drywall, moisture-resistant boards, or custom storage framing make the most sense. When Professional Guidance Helps: Having an experienced general contractor prevents costly mistakes with ventilation or code requirements. Abraham Becerra at HH Remodeling LLC manages garage remodeling throughout Denver and surrounding areas. Call 303-505-0866 to schedule a consultation.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-23"
}